      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Assessments for installation by 3 installers began early in March with much too and fro on various fitouts-prices/quotes. Final installation was in late May. The time taken was largely due to my requirements. Being situated in a regional area there were limited equipment/ brand combinations available from locals (e.g Tindo panels would have required an extra-large deposit). Western Power/Synergy only allow residences to have a maximum 6.6kW of panels and a 5kW Inverter. They also require emergency disconnection from the Grid.Electric Cool were able to supply my 2nd preference combination of:16 REC alpha pure R 410 W panels, 5kW Fronius Genn 24 primo Inverter, Fronius smart meter and Clenergy racking.The location was to a shed roof in one single string facing Northwest with 11degrees of pitch.With wireless internet to the property and WiFi (located 70 metres away in the home), I had to run a separate internet cable to the shed in order to penetrate the Faraday effect of the iron shed cladding. Few changes were necessary to the main power board in the shed.Electric Cool was chosen as the knowledgeable first contact and had a willingness to meet my requirements with continued good communications.The company had just begun using the Open Solar/ Nearmaps system of presenting the quote and associated performance information. This system was not truly representative of my installation (I found this to be common with other quotes). I suggested a simple analysis based on SolarQuotes \"Comprehensive Quote\".Electric Cool said that they were to work on the system and data supplied with quotes.Throughout the process the company conveyed acceptance of feedback and the installation was completed by the team in a professional manner (the company has a lifetime warranty on its workmanship).Since installation we have had a cool overcast and rainy month of June and the system has been performing as expected.",
